<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="legs-for-protection-warrior-tank">Legs for Protection Warrior Tank</h4>Similarly to the gloves slot, the <span class="c1">Protection</span> <a class="icontiny c1" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/class=1/warrior">
<img alt="Warrior" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warrior.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Warrior</span></a> ilvl 378 T12 legs <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=70942/legguards-of-the-molten-giant">
<img alt="Legguards of the Molten Giant" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_pants_raidwarrior_j_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Legguards of the Molten Giant</span></a> are the best legs available outside of raid for <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a>. They come with perfect secondary stats for a tank and are also the biggest upgrade over the next best item for this phase so a wise purchase for your <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a>. Ultimately, they will be upgraded to <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71607">ilvl 391</a> version and never leave your BiS setup.<br/>
<br/>The ilvl 372 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=63501/thunder-wall-greaves">
<img alt="Thunder Wall Greaves" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_raidwarrior_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Thunder Wall Greaves</span></a> <b>-of the Bedrock</b> or <b>-of the Rockslab</b> — which can be randomly acquired from the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=232972/satchel-of-the-thunder-wall-greaves">
<img alt="Satchel of the Thunder Wall Greaves" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bag_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Satchel of the Thunder Wall Greaves</span></a> bought for 12 <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a> — are technically speaking the next best item. However, I recommend against spending your precious <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a> on this item since there are much higher priority items to get first and you should instead buy the T12 legs with your first <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a>.<br/>
<br/>In the meantime, the T11 legs <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=60330/earthen-legguards">
<img alt="Earthen Legguards" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_raidwarrior_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Earthen Legguards</span></a> can be bought with <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a> until you gather enough <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a>. Although they don't come with mastery, the large amount of parry can be reforged into mastery to bandaid this shortcoming so they remain decent legs. <br/>
<br/>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=69583/legguards-of-the-unforgiving">
<img alt="Legguards of the Unforgiving" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_28.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Legguards of the Unforgiving</span></a> introduced with Phase 2 are a good alternative to the T11 legs thanks to better secondary stats in spite of the lower item level. Unfortunately, the gem sockets are pretty bad so the T11 legs remain the best item for the legs slot. But since troll dungeons don't reward <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a>, I don't recommend wasting your time in there.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Leg Armor:</b> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71720/drakehide-leg-armor">
<img alt="Drakehide Leg Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cataclysmarmorkit_08.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Drakehide Leg Armor</span></a>
