<div class="pad"></div>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="rings-for-protection-warrior-tank">Rings for Protection Warrior Tank</h4>With the addition of the <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a>, the ring slots are dominated by the ilvl 372 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=65372/permafrost-signet">
<img alt="Permafrost Signet" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_86.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Permafrost Signet</span></a> <b>-of the Rockslab</b> or <b>-of the Bedrock</b> and ilvl 379 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=60226/dargonaxs-signet">
<img alt="Dargonax's Signet" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_rubystar.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dargonax's Signet</span></a> originally from <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=45213/sinestra">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sinestra</span></a>, on par with ilvl 391 rings from heroic <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5723/firelands">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Firelands</span></a> thanks to their additional gem socket over the competition at no cost to the total item budget for being a <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=45213/sinestra">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sinestra</span></a> drop. The former can be quickly acquired from the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=232959/satchel-of-the-permafrost-signet">
<img alt="Satchel of the Permafrost Signet" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bag_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Satchel of the Permafrost Signet</span></a> for only 12 <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a>, while the <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=45213/sinestra">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Sinestra</span></a> ring will take more effort at 80 <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a> but will last you a long time.<br/>
<br/>In the meantime, the ilvl 365 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=70127/lylagar-horn-ring">
<img alt="Lylagar Horn Ring" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_65.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lylagar Horn Ring</span></a> is a good pick-up with excellent tank secondary stats, if you already grinded the <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5733/molten-front">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Molten Front</span></a> zone to unlock the vendor <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=53882/varlan-highbough">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Varlan Highbough</span></a>. The also excellent <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=58187/ring-of-the-battle-anthem">
<img alt="Ring of the Battle Anthem" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_82.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ring of the Battle Anthem</span></a> can now be bought with <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a> while you grind heroics for <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a>.<br/>
<br/>The <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/skill=755/jewelcrafting">
<img alt="Jewelcrafting" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Jewelcrafting</span></a> crafts <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52320/elementium-moebius-band">
<img alt="Elementium Moebius Band" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_69.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Elementium Moebius Band</span></a> are great rings to buy as soon as you hit max level, thanks to a decent amount of mastery paired with a second defensive stat and an additional gem socket at no cost to their item budget, which brings its total stats dangerously close to the ilvl 359 epics available in Phase 1 raids. Since the <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52320/elementium-moebius-band">
<img alt="Elementium Moebius Band" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_69.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Elementium Moebius Band</span></a> is surprisingly not unique-equipped, you can equip two of them at the same time.<br/>
<i>The <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=69852/punishers-band">
<img alt="Punisher's Band" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_70.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Punisher's Band</span></a> and <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52348/elementium-destroyers-ring">
<img alt="Elementium Destroyer's Ring" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_70.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Elementium Destroyer's Ring</span></a> are technically the next best rings, also with high mastery and the additional gem socket, but there is no point in spending the money for those lesser crafts when you can equip 2x <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52320/elementium-moebius-band">
<img alt="Elementium Moebius Band" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_69.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Elementium Moebius Band</span></a>.</i>
<br/>
<br/>If you don't feel like spending gold on high-level <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/skill=755/jewelcrafting">
<img alt="Jewelcrafting" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Jewelcrafting</span></a> crafts for ephemeral pre-raid gear, there are many great and easy-to-get alternatives. The <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56398/ring-of-three-lights">
<img alt="Ring of Three Lights" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_77.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ring of Three Lights</span></a> and <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=62351/felsens-ring-of-resolve">
<img alt="Felsen's Ring of Resolve" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_26.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Felsen's Ring of Resolve</span></a> are basically identical and with perfect tank stats. The <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=62440/red-rock-band">
<img alt="Red Rock Band" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_kingsring1.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Red Rock Band</span></a> and <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56444/umbriss-band">
<img alt="Umbriss Band" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_stonering2.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Umbriss Band</span></a> are ever so slightly worse because of their expertise/<wbr/>hit ratings but come with a lot more baseline mastery entirely making up for it. <br/>
<br/>The rings introduced in Phase 2, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=69563/ring-of-the-numberless-brood">
<img alt="Ring of the Numberless Brood" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_zulgurub_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Ring of the Numberless Brood</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=69553/talonguard-band">
<img alt="Talonguard Band" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_ring_14.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Talonguard Band</span></a>, are worse than the ilvl 346 blue rings listed below due to mediocre secondary stats.<div class="pad"></div>
