<div class="pad"></div>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="trinkets-for-protection-warrior-tank">Trinkets for Protection Warrior Tank</h4>With the addition of the <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a>s in Phase 3, you can now buy the ilvl 372 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=65048/symbiotic-worm">
<img alt="Symbiotic Worm" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_qiraj_skinsandworm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Symbiotic Worm</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=65109/vial-of-stolen-memories">
<img alt="Vial of Stolen Memories" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cat_trinket02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vial of Stolen Memories</span></a>, the best trinkets of Phases 1 &amp; 2, for 50 <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a> each which is a bargain. Both are excellent versatile, equip-and-forget trinkets with a large stack of stamina to raise your survivability against any type of incoming damage. As the cherry on top, the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=65048/symbiotic-worm">
<img alt="Symbiotic Worm" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_qiraj_skinsandworm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Symbiotic Worm</span></a> comes with great emergency proc <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=92356">raising your mastery significantly when your health dips below 35%</a>.<br/>
<br/>Next on the list of must-haves is the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=62471/mirror-of-broken-images">
<img alt="Mirror of Broken Images" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_platnumdisks.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mirror of Broken Images</span></a>. The Mirror is more of a situational trinket that shines against magic tank busters specifically, thanks to its excellent on-use <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=92222/image-of-immortality">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_antimagicshell.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Image of Immortality</span></a> providing high magic damage mitigation on a short cooldown, reminiscent of the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=50364/sindragosas-flawless-fang">
<img alt="Sindragosa's Flawless Fang" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sindragosa's Flawless Fang</span></a> from Wrath. Stamina in place of Mastery would have made this trinket perfect against magic damage, since our mastery <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=76857/critical-block">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_criticalblock.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Critical Block</span></a> only affects physical damage.  This one might be a painful grind since it requires reaching Exalted with the <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/faction=1177/baradins-wardens">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Baradin's Wardens</span></a>/<wbr/>
<a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/faction=1178/hellscreams-reach">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Hellscream's Reach</span></a> PvP reputations via dailies and PvP events, but well worth the effort.<br/>
<br/>The only new trinket worth mentioning for Phase 3 is the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=70143/moonwell-phial">
<img alt="Moonwell Phial" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_alchemy_imbuedvial.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Moonwell Phial</span></a>, which can be bought from <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=53881/ayla-shadowstorm">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ayla Shadowstorm</span></a> in the <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5733/molten-front">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Molten Front</span></a> zone after unlocking this vendor. It also comes with a lot of stamina to raise your survivability against any type of incoming damage, paired with a long <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=101492">20-second +1700 dodge rating bonus</a> compared to the usual 10-15 second effect of similar pre-raid trinkets, with the caveat that you must stay inside the 10-yard radius pool of water that the trinket spawns on the ground to maintain the bonus.<br/>
<br/>The best ilvl 346 to pick-up while you're farming heroics is the trusty <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56347/leaden-despair">
<img alt="Leaden Despair" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/quest_12252_icon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leaden Despair</span></a>. It's a fantastic trinket, also with a big stack of stamina useful against every damage type, paired with arguably the best type of emergency procs <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=92185">providing reliable damage mitigation when your health dips low</a>.<br/>
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56280/porcelain-crab">
<img alt="Porcelain Crab" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_purplecrab.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Porcelain Crab</span></a> is another good pre-raid trinket thanks to a ~20% uptime of the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=92175">mastery rating proc</a> <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=92174/hardened-shell">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_shell_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Hardened Shell</span></a>.<div class="box" data-level="null">
<ul class="first last">
<li class="fa fa-warning">
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>During the two weeks of the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/guide/holidays/brewfest-guide">Brewfest event</a> only</b>, you can obtain the two tank trinkets <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=232016/bubblier-brightbrew-charm">
<img alt="Bubblier Brightbrew Charm" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_drink_08.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bubblier Brightbrew Charm</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=232017/bitterer-balebrew-charm">
<img alt="Bitterer Balebrew Charm" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_drink_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bitterer Balebrew Charm</span></a> from <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=23872/coren-direbrew">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Coren Direbrew</span></a> in the Grim Guzzler pub of <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=1584/blackrock-depths">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Blackrock Depths</span></a>. These catch-up trinkets have been nerfed for Classic due to the event releasing before <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5723/firelands">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Firelands</span></a>, from ilvl 365 down to ilvl 353.<br/>As a result, they only give an extra 29 stamina over the ilvl 346 <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56347/leaden-despair">
<img alt="Leaden Despair" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/quest_12252_icon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leaden Despair</span></a>, which is decent against magic damage but the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=92185/item-proc-armor">emergency armor proc</a> keeps <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56347/leaden-despair">
<img alt="Leaden Despair" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/quest_12252_icon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leaden Despair</span></a> ahead of both ilvl 353 trinkets for physical and hybrid damage profiles.<br/>That being said, the Brewfest trinkets are a great pick-up while you work towards unlocking <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=53881/ayla-shadowstorm">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Ayla Shadowstorm</span></a> in the <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5733/molten-front">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Molten Front</span></a> zone to buy the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=70143/moonwell-phial">
<img alt="Moonwell Phial" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_alchemy_imbuedvial.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Moonwell Phial</span></a>. Their on-use effect, summoning respectively <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=54337/the-brewmaiden">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Brewmaiden</span></a> which heals you for a low amount during 35 seconds, and <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=54336/the-black-brewmaiden">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Black Brewmaiden</span></a> smacking your target with her tankards, can help a little bit in solo situations primarily. They have a long 10-minute cooldown so get both trinkets and cycle them while they are on cooldown.</div></li></ul></div>
<ul>
<li class="fa fa-warning">
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Trinkets to avoid</b>
<br/>The <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/skill=171/alchemy">
<img alt="Alchemy" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_alchemy.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Alchemy</span></a> exclusive <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=58483/lifebound-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Lifebound Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_aspiration.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lifebound Alchemist Stone</span></a> is <i>technically speaking</i> the third best pre-raid trinket. However, the weaker <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/skill=171/alchemy">
<img alt="Alchemy" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_alchemy.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Alchemy</span></a> profession perks compared to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/skill=165/leatherworking">
<img alt="Leatherworking" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_armorkit_17.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leatherworking</span></a> entirely <ins>offset the benefits</ins> of this trinket so I don't recommend leveling this profession as a <span class="c1">Protection</span> <a class="icontiny c1" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/class=1/warrior">
<img alt="Warrior" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warrior.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Warrior</span></a>. Moreover, there are no upgrades to the Alchemist stones in Cataclysm compared to previous expansions so this trinket is an ephemeral investment.<br/>In the same vein, the <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/skill=755/jewelcrafting">
<img alt="Jewelcrafting" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Jewelcrafting</span></a> trinket <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52352/figurine-earthen-guardian">
<img alt="Figurine - Earthen Guardian" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_earthenmight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Figurine - Earthen Guardian</span></a> is also a great pickup before starting raids, but once again, the average profession perks of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/skill=755/jewelcrafting">
<img alt="Jewelcrafting" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Jewelcrafting</span></a> compared to <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/skill=165/leatherworking">
<img alt="Leatherworking" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_armorkit_17.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Leatherworking</span></a> offset that gain entirely.<br/>While trinkets with bonus armor were among the best options in previous expansions, they have been severely nerfed in Cataclysm. As a result, the ilvl 359 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=58182/bedrock-talisman">
<img alt="Bedrock Talisman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_armorkit_21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bedrock Talisman</span></a> bought with <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=395/justice-points">
<span>
<img alt="Justice Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-justice.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justice Points</span></span></a> is only a mediocre choice below the <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56280/porcelain-crab">
<img alt="Porcelain Crab" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_purplecrab.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Porcelain Crab</span></a> and a poor use of your currencies.</div></li></ul>
