<a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/npc=43875/asaad">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Asaad</span></a></td>
<td>
<a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5035/the-vortex-pinnacle">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Vortex Pinnacle</span></a> <span class="icon-heroic"></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<br/>
<hr/>
<br/>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="weapons">Weapons for Protection Warrior Tank</h3>
<div class="pad"></div>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="main-hand-weapons-for-protection-warrior-tank">Main Hand Weapons for Protection Warrior Tank</h4>
<ul>
<li class="fa fa-arrow-right">
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<i>While your choice of weapon was possibly the most intricate part of gearing a tank in previous expansions, with different speeds for different usage and preferred weapon types based on your talents, or race and unique weapon proficiencies, all of these nuances go out of the window with the new expansion. <b>In Cataclysm</b>, 99% of main-hands with strength are the same 2.60 speed tank-oriented weapons and the bonus expertise from <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=20597/sword-specialization">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_meleedamage.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sword Specialization</span></a> or <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=20574/axe-specialization">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_axe_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Axe Specialization</span></a> barely amount to a 1-2% TPS difference that we will mostly ignore to focus on better survivability since threat is no longer a concern.</i></div></li></ul>
<b>Phase 3</b> introduces 3 new epic ilvl 365 weapons all crafted by <a class="icontiny" data-entity="skill" data-game="wow" data-type="skill" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/skill=164/blacksmithing">
<img alt="Blacksmithing" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_blacksmithing.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blacksmithing</span></a> with plans that can be bought from the unlockable vendors of the <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5733/molten-front">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Molten Front</span></a> zone. For this reason, expect these crafts to only become available 3 to 4 weeks after the release of the <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5733/molten-front">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Molten Front</span></a> zone.<br/>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=70163/unbreakable-guardian">
<img alt="Unbreakable Guardian" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_1h_cataclysm_c_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unbreakable Guardian</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=70158/elementium-edged-scalper">
<img alt="Elementium-Edged Scalper" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_axe_1h_pvp400_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Elementium-Edged Scalper</span></a> are both valid choices, with the former providing ~1.2% more survivability while the latter provides ~0.6% more threat. I would craft the sword out of the two, unless you are an <a class="icontiny" data-entity="race" data-game="wow" data-type="race" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/race=2/orc">
<img alt="Orc" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_orc_male.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Orc</span></a> <a class="icontiny c1" data-entity="class" data-game="wow" data-type="class" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/class=1/warrior">
<img alt="Warrior" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warrior.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Warrior</span></a> in which case the additional expertise can tip the balance in favor of the axe. The last option, the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=70162/pyrium-spellward">
<img alt="Pyrium Spellward" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_1h_cataclysm_c_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Pyrium Spellward</span></a>, isn't an upgrade despite its higher item level and weapon DPS due to agility instead of strength as a primary stat.<br/>
<br/>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=59347/mace-of-acrid-death">
<img alt="Mace of Acrid Death" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_mace_1h_bwdraid_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mace of Acrid Death</span></a> from Phase 1 can also now be bought for 20 <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a>. However, it's only a downgrade to the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=70163/unbreakable-guardian">
<img alt="Unbreakable Guardian" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_1h_cataclysm_c_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Unbreakable Guardian</span></a> at ilvl 359 with identical stats, so it's best to save your <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a>s for much bigger upgrades in this list, unless the materials to craft these new catch-up <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5733/molten-front">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Molten Front</span></a> weapons are too expensive on your realm.<br/>All in all, both the ilvl 365 and ilvl 359 weapons are only slight upgrades compared to the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=69609/bloodlords-protector">
<img alt="Bloodlord's Protector" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_54.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bloodlord's Protector</span></a> or <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56346/elementium-fang">
<img alt="Elementium Fang" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_1h_cataclysm_c_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Elementium Fang</span></a> from previous phases, so they should be a low priority. <br/>
<br/>Phase 2 introduced 4 new epic swords from <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=1977/zulgurub">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Zul'Gurub</span></a> and <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=3805/zulaman">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Zul'Aman</span></a>, however, only the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=69609/bloodlords-protector">
<img alt="Bloodlord's Protector" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_54.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bloodlord's Protector</span></a> and the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=69639/renatakis-soul-slicer">
<img alt="Renataki's Soul Slicer" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_31.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Renataki's Soul Slicer</span></a> could be considered upgrades to the already excellent <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56346/elementium-fang">
<img alt="Elementium Fang" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_1h_cataclysm_c_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Elementium Fang</span></a>. Despite the lack of mastery, the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=69609/bloodlords-protector">
<img alt="Bloodlord's Protector" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_54.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bloodlord's Protector</span></a> is a slight upgrade for survivability thanks to its superior item level and double tank secondary stats, and the higher DPS improves TPS by ~0.6% at no loss over <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56346/elementium-fang">
<img alt="Elementium Fang" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_1h_cataclysm_c_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Elementium Fang</span></a>. The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=69639/renatakis-soul-slicer">
<img alt="Renataki's Soul Slicer" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_31.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Renataki's Soul Slicer</span></a>, on the other hand, does come with mastery but the DPS-oriented secondary stats still lead to a survivability loss of ~0.8% in exchange for a TPS increase of ~1.3%. <br/>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=69618/zulian-slasher">
<img alt="Zulian Slasher" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_77.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zulian Slasher</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=70080/reforged-heartless">
<img alt="Reforged Heartless" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_107.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reforged Heartless</span></a> are too big of a downgrade in survivability to be considered over <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56346/elementium-fang">
<img alt="Elementium Fang" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_1h_cataclysm_c_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Elementium Fang</span></a> for their marginal TPS upgrade, and overall provide less TPS and less survivability than <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=65171/cookies-tenderizer">
<img alt="Cookie's Tenderizer" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_fabric_silk_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cookie's Tenderizer</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>The best pre-raid weapon in Phase 1 is the <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56346/elementium-fang">
<img alt="Elementium Fang" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_1h_cataclysm_c_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Elementium Fang</span></a>, regardless of race and weapon proficiencies, because it's the only 346 weapon that comes with mastery and avoidance as secondary stats to improve your CTC.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Weapon Enchants</b>: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=74244/enchant-weapon-windwalk">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_enchant_formulasuperior_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Enchant Weapon - Windwalk</span></a>
