<div class="pad"></div>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="ranged-weapons-for-protection-warrior-tank">Ranged Weapons for Protection Warrior Tank</h4>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71077/extreme-impact-hole-puncher">
<img alt="Extreme-Impact Hole Puncher" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_rifle_44.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Extreme-Impact Hole Puncher</span></a>, introduced with the <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/zone=5733/molten-front">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Molten Front</span></a> zone, is the new best pre-raid ranged weapon for a tank, as well as the best ranged weapon for this phase, including heroic raid drops. This is mainly due to its exclusive gem socket which instantly provides 50% more stamina than the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=69637/gurubashi-destroyer">
<img alt="Gurubashi Destroyer" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_firearm_2h_rifle_zulgurub_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gurubashi Destroyer</span></a>. Because the ranged slot provides few stats, a gem socket is a massive jump in stats relatively, which puts this weapon ahead of the competition despite the primary stat being agility instead of strength.<br/>That being said, the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71077/extreme-impact-hole-puncher">
<img alt="Extreme-Impact Hole Puncher" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_weapon_rifle_44.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Extreme-Impact Hole Puncher</span></a> remains a relatively small ~0.5% upgrade in survivability at the scale of your entire gear, so don't break the bank on this craft if the materials are expensive on your realm.<br/>
<br/>The <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=69637/gurubashi-destroyer">
<img alt="Gurubashi Destroyer" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_firearm_2h_rifle_zulgurub_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gurubashi Destroyer</span></a> introduced in Phase 2 is still a great choice. It comes with perfect tank stats but it's only a small upgrade to <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56376/thundercall">
<img alt="Thundercall" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_firearm_2h_rifle_cataclysm_c_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Thundercall</span></a> considering the 7 item level difference only between these two items.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Scope</b>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=59595/r19-threatfinder">
<img alt="R19 Threatfinder" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_scopec.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">R19 Threatfinder</span></a>
